diately upstream of the S01->S04 inline amplifier would explain O1, with unchanged pump current expected because the amplifier itself need not have failed. A second concurrent path failure would still be required to explain O2 and the wider outage.", "grounded": ["oms.S01-S04.span0"], "n_grounded": 1, "note": ""}, {"fault_mode": "OTN_SWITCH_FAIL", "location_kind": "element", "term": null, "anchor_symptom": null, "anchor_service": null, "element": "S01", "probability": 0.03, "rationale": "A switch-fabric failure at the common S01 dependency could interrupt many ODUs simultaneously. However, it would not normally cause the observed AMP_INPUT_LOS and OCH_LOS optical alarms, so it is substantially less likely than the ROADM fault.", "grounded": [], "n_grounded": 0, "note": "site named; its node equipment does not document the mode"}, {"fault_mode": "CONNECTOR_PULLED", "location_kind": "term", "term": "oms_input", "anchor_symptom": "O2", "anchor_service": null, "element": null, "probability": 0.01, "rationale": "A disconnected OMS input patch could create a hard optical loss, but a single patch would generally affect one outgoing section and should be visible at its booster input. The unchanged S01->S15 booster powers and simultaneous loss on S01->S04 argue strongly against it.", "grounded": ["oms.S01-S15"], "n_grounded": 1, "note": ""}], "probability_other": 0.05, "sum_stated": 1.0}, "llm": {"provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-5.6"}, "llm_calls": [{"role": "proposer", "latency_s": 19.01806879043579, "input_tokens": 20954, "output_tokens": 1634, "reasoning_tokens": 1034, "ok": true, "error": ""}]}